What to poly into:

Poly into Giant Shoggoth to kill One Eyed Sam (takes two rounds).
Poly into Giant Shoggoth to clean Vecna's level (make sure to stand on
'E' square).
Poly into Vampire Mage for extra fast healing, flying and drain
resistance.
Poly to Hill orc right off the bat for 18/** strength.
Poly to Yellow light/giant to remove/destroy cursed armor.
Poly to leprachun wizard to steal money back from priest.
Poly to demon to get foocubus as pet.
Poly into black dragon for insta-kill range weapon.


Early drink from sinks for the poly effect (dangerous).

I actually prefer a ring of poly to an amulet of unchanging
in the mid-game (which are the only ones where it is
important - afterwards you're more powerful in your regular
form).  It continually allows you to try and poly to something
new.  Because it activates every few hundred turns, you
can statistically stay polymorphed into even a crystal golem
for quite a while (caution urged with Vecna/etc.).  Plus
you get the advantage of healing (every time you poly),
and being killed in poly'ed form isn't permanent.

